# NOTE: root package-lock.json IS committed (not ignored) on purpose.
# GoDaddy's PaaS build step checks for a lockfile at the repo root to decide
# whether to run install/build at all — no lockfile there means it skips
# straight to the serve command against a server.js that was never built.
# See commit history for the incident this caused.

# Supabase CLI local state (linked project ref, pooler URL, server versions).
# Machine-specific and re-created by `supabase link` — never committed.
supabase/.temp/
